        "research:audit-existing-performance-and-customer-data": false,
        "research:validate-demand-and-willingness-to-pay": true
      },
      "recommendation": "Proceed",
      "notes": "• 14 interviews with in-house marketers and freelancers (Sep–Oct): 11 said they 'retry prompts 3+ times' for ad copy; 9 had never compared tools for a task.\n• Alternatives: prompt libraries (PromptBase, AIPRM), generic ChatGPT 'improve my prompt', internal playbooks. None scores tool-fit for the goal.\n• Waitlist: 640 sign-ups from 2 LinkedIn posts; 23% opened the beta invite and scored ≥3 prompts.\n• WTP: 7 of 14 interviewees would pay $15–25/mo; teams prefer seats + shared prompt library.\n• Open questions: retention after the 'aha' moment; whether agencies are a better secondary ICP than in-house teams.\n• Baseline audit not done yet — no historical funnel data (new product)."
    },
    "positioning": {
      "icp": "In-house B2B/B2C marketer at a 10–200 person company, uses 3+ AI tools weekly for content, ads and creative, measured on output volume and campaign performance.",
      "secondary": "Freelance marketers and small agencies (1–10 people) who deliver AI-assisted work to clients and need consistent quality.",
      "buyer": "PLG: user = buyer for Pro. Team plan: marketing lead buys, team members use.",
      "pain": "Wasting time retrying prompts and using the wrong AI tool for the job; no way to know if AI output is 'good' or how to improve the input.",
      "alternative": "Trial and error in ChatGPT/Claude, prompt libraries (PromptBase, AIPRM), YouTube prompt courses, colleagues' Notion pages.",
      "value": "Know in 30 seconds how good your prompt and tool choice are — and exactly what to change.",
      "differentiation": "Scores the whole setup (goal + context + tool + prompt), not just the prompt text; recommends a better-fit tool when relevant; rubric built by a marketer for marketing tasks.",
      "proof": "Beta: average prompt score rose from 54 to 78 after 3 scored prompts (n=148); 640-person waitlist; founder with 9 years in adtech/marketing.",
      "message": "Stop guessing with AI. Score your prompt, fix it, ship better work.",
      "cta": "Score your first prompt free",
      "objections": "'ChatGPT can improve my prompt for free' → it rewrites text but doesn't evaluate tool-fit or score against marketing goals.\n'Is my prompt data safe?' → prompts aren't used for training; delete-anytime; clear privacy page.\n'$19 is a lot for a prompt tool' → one saved hour a month pays for it; free tier covers 10 scores/month.\n'My team has its own playbook' → Team plan lets you score against your own playbook rules (roadmap)."
    },
